  "final_message": "I have initiated the directory listing command and will examine the workspace structure once it finishes.\nI have started running `npm test` and will check the output once it finishes.\nI have started searching the oracle for references to `X-remove` and will review the output once it finishes.\nI have launched `npm test` and will check the output once it finishes.\nI have started `npm run typecheck && npm run arch` and will verify the results once the command completes.\nI am waiting for the typecheck and architecture verification to finish.\nI have launched the typecheck and architecture verification command and will wait for it to finish.\nI did not remove `channel` from [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/orders-service/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) or the order model.\n\nWhile `channel` is no longer actively used internally within `orders-service`, the downstream consumer repository [`analytics-ingest`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/analytics-ingest/README.md) (team Data) explicitly depends on `channel` in its contract for [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts#L7-L13):\n- [`decodeOrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts#L25-L46) strictly validates that `channel` is present and one of `\"web\" | \"store\" | \"marketplace\"`, throwing `ContractViolationError` if missing.\n- It records `channel` directly into the `orders` lake table in [`ingestOrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/analytics-ingest/src/ingest.ts#L17-L27).\n\nRemoving `channel` from the event would break the deployed consumer contract. Instead, I marked the field as `@deprecated` in [events.ts](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/orders-service/src/core/events.ts#L16-L20) so that it can be decommissioned once team Data updates `analytics-ingest`.\n",
